  "difficulty": "easy",
  "topics": ["two-pointers", "strings"],
  "source": "canonical Valid Palindrome concept; description, examples, and tests re-authored",
  "description": "A palindrome reads the same forward and backward. Return True if s is a palindrome once you keep only its letters and digits and ignore letter case, and False otherwise. A string that becomes empty after filtering counts as a palindrome.",
  "constraints": [
    "0 <= len(s) <= 20000",
    "s consists of printable ASCII characters"
  ],
  "parameters": ["s"],
  "functionName": "is_palindrome",
  "starterCode": "def is_palindrome(s):\n    # Return True if s, keeping only letters and digits and ignoring case, is a palindrome.\n    ...\n",
  "examples": [
    {
      "input": { "s": "Never odd or even" },
      "output": true,
      "explanation": "keeping only letters gives neveroddoreven, which reads the same both ways"
    },
    {
      "input": { "s": "Hello, world" },
      "output": false,
      "explanation": "helloworld does not read the same backward"
    }
  ],
  "hints": [
    "Filter first: decide which characters actually participate in the comparison.",
    "You can compare characters from both ends and meet in the middle instead of building new strings.",
    "Keep two indices, left and right. Skip characters that are not letters or digits, compare lowercased characters, and move inward; any mismatch means False."
  ],
  "solution": "Use two indices moving inward from both ends. Skip characters that are not letters or digits, compare lowercased characters, and return False on any mismatch. When the indices cross, the string is a palindrome. One pass: O(n) time, O(1) extra space.",
  "solutionCode": "def is_palindrome(s):\n    left = 0\n    right = len(s) - 1\n    while left < right:\n        if not s[left].isalnum():\n            left += 1\n        elif not s[right].isalnum():\n            right -= 1\n        elif s[left].lower() != s[right].lower():\n            return False\n        else:\n            left += 1\n            right -= 1\n    return True\n",
  "bruteForceCode": "def is_palindrome(s):\n    filtered = \"\"\n    for ch in s:\n        if ch.isalnum():\n            filtered += ch.lower()\n    reversed_text = \"\"\n    for ch in filtered:\n        reversed_text = ch + reversed_text\n    return filtered == reversed_text\n",
  "failureHint": "hidden tests include empty and symbol-only strings, digits, and one very long palindrome",
  "parTimeSec": 300,
  "expectedComplexity": { "time": "O(n)", "space": "O(1)" },
